title: Sort groups
intro: A thing made of several sprites, a stack of crates on a pallet, can now sort by Y as one, so a character walks in front of the whole stack or behind all of it.
project: Empty | Warehouse

chapter: A stack on a pallet | Each part sorts at its own feet
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Sort By Y = true
agent: entity_create {"entity": {"name": "Pallet", "position": [0, 0], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#8A5A3A", "size": [1.6, 0.4]}}, "children": [{"name": "Crate 1", "position": [0, 0.4], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#4870E0", "size": [1.2, 0.4]}}}, {"name": "Crate 2", "position": [0, 0.8], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#5880F0", "size": [1.2, 0.4]}}}, {"name": "Crate 3", "position": [0, 1.2], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#4870E0", "size": [1.2, 0.4]}}}, {"name": "Crate 4", "position": [0, 1.6], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#5880F0", "size": [1.2, 0.4]}}}]}}
agent: entity_create {"entity": {"name": "Worker", "position": [0, 0.9], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#E04848", "size": [0.6, 1.2]}}}}
look: 0, 0.6, 2.5
say: The camera sorts by Y, as a top-down game's does: what stands lower down draws in front. Here's a pallet with four crates stacked on it, each its own sprite, and a worker standing behind it.
play
expectdrawn: 0, 1.2 = #E04848
expectdrawn: 0, 0.4 = #4870E0
stop
explain: entity:Worker | Caught in the stack | Each crate sorts at its own feet, and the higher ones stand higher up the screen, so the worker draws over the top crates and under the bottom one, as if standing inside the stack.

chapter: Sort Group | One entry at the pallet's feet
select: Pallet
add: Sort Group
explain: component:SortGroup | Sort Group | A Sort Group on the pallet makes it and everything inside it sort as one thing, at the pallet's feet. Inside the group, the parts draw by their own Order, then in Hierarchy order: bottom crate to top.
play
expectdrawn: 0, 1.2 = #4870E0
stop
explain: entity:Pallet | Behind the whole stack | Standing above the pallet's feet, the worker is now behind every crate.
select: Worker
set: Transform.Position = 0, -0.5, 0
play
expectdrawn: 0, 0 = #E04848
stop
explain: entity:Worker | In front of all of it | One step lower, and the worker draws over the whole stack. Ground Offset moves the point the group sorts at, for a root drawn with space under its feet, and a tilemap's walls sorting by Y interleave with groups as with any sprite.
